        "text": "chown\nThe chown command is used to change the owner and group of a given file or directory. To change\nthe owner and group of a directory, we must pass both arguments separated by the : sign. Just like\nthe chmod command, you can replicate the new settings recursively by adding -R to the command:\nFigure 2.16 \u2013 Changing the owner and group of a directory\nThis command changes the owner and group of the directory located at /home/instructor/\nDocuments/office-docs/ along with all its content recursively. The -R option stands for recursive .",
